+# Exhibits 336/337: the indexed French-information controls and the missing source joins
+
+Research date: October 30, 2026, America/New_York. The user requested comparison of court exhibits **336 and 337 against 326, 636, 637 and 639**. Both new PDFs were acquired from the actual links in the [official court index](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense.html); all eleven physical pages were inspected visually, and all four held single-page controls were reinspected without redownloading. The [preceding review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/3f50f2c6904eca6a39efa4c06c15ea838729a65d/investigation/broader-evidence/moussaoui-reply-update-2026-10-30/README.md) had listed 336/337 as unexamined candidate controls, not authenticated missing French intelligence attachments.
+
+**The useful new finding is a source-identification limit and a specific missing-report pointer.** The court index labels both exhibits as French information, but 336 contains an August 21 request/cover note and identification/photo material, while 337 contains a web-profile printout about Masood Al-Benin. These copies do not establish the underlying French/CIA assessment, its exact contents or its receipt by a particular reviewer. Preserve the index descriptions and actual contents side by side; the broad labels alone neither authenticate an attachment join nor establish a cataloguing error, concealment or substitution.
+
+## What is actually in 336
+
+The [six-page 336 PDF](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/336.pdf#page=1) has the following physical-page inventory. These are page roles within one court exhibit, not six independent confirmations. Pins F01–F03 in [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) give visible anchors and production marks.
+
+| Physical PDF page | Readable contents | Limit |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 1 | English cover note dated **21 August 2001**; says an FBI investigation report and photographs are attached; requests information listed on the report's **page 7** | Recipient/source fields are masked. This is a request/attachment description, not a French substantive intelligence reply or proof of receipt |
+| 2 | Identification/passport-image page, with a LEGAT-PARIS image-print header | Identity particulars, portrait and signatures are excluded from this public derivative; their presence does not authenticate the transmission |
+| 3 | Very dark photo/image page with a LEGAT-PARIS print header | Central image content cannot be reliably identified from this rendition; no enhancement, hidden-layer recovery or face comparison performed |
+| 4 | Another identification/photo page with a LEGAT-PARIS print header | Same privacy and authentication limits; do not infer which photo was used by a recipient |
+| 5 | Sideways working-copy rendition of the **21 August 2001** cover note, repeating the attached-report and page-7 request | Same substantive request wording detected visually; layout/marking differences retained. No native/pixel identity or separate completed action inferred |
+| 6 | Sideways working-copy continuation containing an FBI ownership/distribution disclaimer | This is not the requested investigative report page 7 |
+
+**The attached report's requested page 7 was not identified among the readable contents of this six-page PDF.** Physical PDF count and an internal reference to a different attached report are different things. The dark page remains unreadable; this is not a finding about hidden contents, a complete original packet or the full court production. No source page is silently filled in, renumbered, or identified as another held LHM merely because its length or subject seems similar. Pins F01–F03.
+
+The cover's marked and working-copy renditions retain their separate appearances. Classification cancellations, masked fields, image filenames, handwriting and production labels are not treated as authorizations, transmission receipts, authorship proof or wrongdoing. Original pixels/page order and PDF bytes are unchanged. The complete requested report, its page 7, original attachment manifest and dispatch/receipt record are precise TODO inputs.
+
+## What is actually in 337
+
+The [five-page 337 PDF](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/337.pdf#page=1) begins with a French-language title sheet for a profile of **Masood Al-Benin**, followed by four English article/visitor-note printout pages. The heading presents an April 12, 2000 death account. Physical pages 3–4 describe the article subject's reported travel, Chechnya activity and computer/media work; page 5 contains continuation material and visitor/support text, including a **23 April 2000** note. These dates describe the displayed article/note, not an authenticated August 2001 dispatch or reviewer receipt. Pins F04–F05.
+
+This is an article representation inside a court exhibit, **not visibly a French intelligence agency's assessment of Moussaoui**. Its claims remain attributed to the article; they are not independently validated here. In the readable five pages, no direct Moussaoui-to-Khattab-to-bin Laden chain matching the claims in 636/637 was identified. Related geography, militancy, language or web context does not establish identity, personal contact or the specific missing evidentiary association. A person named in the profile must not be conflated with Moussaoui. This is a bounded visual reading, not a search of obscured layers or proof that no relevant counterpart exists elsewhere.
+
+The French title sheet and English printout body retain their different languages and forms. No full bilingual translation, authorship verification, original website/archive validation, native file metadata extraction, capture-date reconstruction or identity matching was performed. The visible footer's file/print context does not supply a proven origin-to-court or intelligence-distribution chain. Raw article pages, contact text, local file paths and portraits are not republished here.
+
+## Comparison with the four held messages
+
+The following preserves source reports separately from what the new copies actually establish. Exact page/header/paragraph anchors are pins F06–F09; all four single-page PDFs were reinspected.
+
+| Held exhibit and source report | Comparison result from 336/337 | Unresolved join |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| [326, page 1](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/326.pdf#page=1): August 16 reply quoting August 15 inquiry; Samit's concern and uncertainty; Abbott's intended write-up/attempted handoff | 336 supplies a later-dated request/cover representation, with photos/identification and an attached-report reference. It is not thereby the exact write-up promised in 326, nor proof the attempted handoff happened | Original write-up/EC, recipient copy, dispatch/receipt and returned checks |
+| [636, page 1](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/636.pdf#page=1): August 24 Samit report attributing a possible bin Laden connection to CIA/CTC assistance and French information | Neither new PDF supplies a readable underlying assessment establishing that asserted association. 336 shows a request; 337 is a web profile about someone else | Original French information and CIA/CTC assessment, with explicit source/package/recipient association |
+| [637, page 1](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/637.pdf#page=1): August 24 request says opening EC and Paris information attached, reports a headquarters sufficiency position, disagrees and seeks a firmer connection | Court PDFs 336/337 do not by themselves identify the exact Paris-information attachment or what legal reviewers saw. Their broad index titles cannot supply the missing manifest | Original thread and attachments, precise reviewed package, advice and actual referral/nonreferral/disposition |
+| [639, page 1](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/639.pdf#page=1): August 24 Maltbie reports earlier photo/bio dissemination, same-day pocket-litter/photos and continuing tasking, alongside caution about planned wrongdoing | 336 is concrete request/photo-material evidence consistent with investigative information-seeking. It does not prove these are the same items reported in 639 or establish recipient receipt/return. 337 provides no demonstrated join to that transmission | Exact photo/bio/pocket-litter packet and task returns; unidentified earlier communication referenced by the caution |
+
+The earlier assessment contrast remains: field concern and attributed possible-link reports coexist with the later caution in 639 and reported continuing tasking. **This review does not resolve why they differ.** Suspicion, a possible association, a demonstrated foreign-power connection, planned wrongdoing, search authority and completed action are different propositions. Different information, different questions/thresholds, tentative reporting or unsupported downplaying remain untested alternatives. No source is silently selected as controlling.
+
+## Evidentiary value and what would change the assessment
+
+**Direct observations, high confidence within readable scope:** these two downloaded PDFs have six and five pages respectively; 336's cover asks for information on a referenced report page 7; the visible new contents are the request/identification material and an article printout, not an identified native French/CIA assessment. Hosting and hashes identify court-served copies, not native documents or the historical truth of every source assertion.
+
+**Useful inference, limited confidence:** the earlier French-information lead remains incomplete. The exact report/page-7 reference and the need to identify the actual source intelligence make the next retrieval more precise. This is narrower than saying no French information existed or that anyone suppressed it. A broad navigation label may have a legitimate exhibit-context explanation; that explanation is not established here either.
+
+**Counterevidence and dependence:** 326's promised checks, 336's express request and 639's reported dissemination/tasking show or report active attempts to obtain/share information. They weigh against a blanket stopped-investigation claim, while leaving actual execution/receipt and adequacy open. The two 336 cover renditions repeat a request rather than independently corroborating its delivery. Same-investigator accounts and an article reused as an attachment also must not be counted as independent proof. Neither the catalogue label nor a production gap proves concealment, unlawful destruction, substitution, coordination or intent.
+
+**Next discriminating inputs:** obtain the full report and its requested page 7, actual original French reply and any translation/attachment manifest; then establish delivery and exact inclusion in the intelligence/legal-review packet. Knowing omission or misstatement of material received information would strengthen a suppression interpretation. A tentative source, absence of the claimed association, inclusion elsewhere, different questions or substantive follow-up could weaken it. Those tests remain unperformed. The court index separately lists 59B as a Legat/French-information memo, 346 as an August 22 information-transmission EC and 642 as an August 30 attachment email; they are **indexed candidate routes, not acquired/read results of this unit**, and earlier acquisition status outside this unit must be checked before repeating a route.
+
+## Preservation, TODOs and verification
+
+[OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) carries forward **DRAFT-T01–T06**, now marking 336/337 acquired and read while leaving native attachments/source intelligence, original interview/advice, exact reviewed packages, receipt/task returns, formal actions and native chronology/assembly open. The previous queue's candidate labels are preserved in the preceding published version; they were not already findings that these were the missing intelligence originals. The all-eighteen-criterion/five-track investigation remains open or partial; this bounded unit does not replace or complete it.
+
+[SOURCES.json](SOURCES.json) records court URLs, actual access UTC/local dates, byte counts, hashes, page counts and source relationships. [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) uses physical PDF pages and visible headers/paragraphs, with line locators only for this report's prose. No invented source-transcript line numbers. [SOURCE-CHECKS.json](SOURCE-CHECKS.json) records actual byte/page/passive-container checks against six held PDF entities and the index. Absence of an embedded-file entry does not prove no attachment existed historically. Those checks do not independently validate manual readings, native authenticity, legal sufficiency or historical conclusions.
+
+**Actual reading:** all eleven new physical pages viewed at longest-dimension 1800-pixel render resolution, including the dark unreadable image and sideways working-copy pages; all four held single pages reinspected. No other full source newly read. No OCR/hidden-text recovery, masked-field reconstruction, image enhancement/face matching, original-language intelligence translation, native-message/clock authentication, underlying web-story validation, legal adjudication or physical test performed. Page count inspected is not a count of legible pages or proof of claims.
+
+[CHECKLIST.md](CHECKLIST.md) accounts for the instructions; [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) is the real Git addition diff against the immediately preceding absent state of these research text files, not a purported native-email version diff. Source/page/layout review is separate from that text diff. Original PDFs, redactions, annotations, page order, prior reports/TODOs and original-scope records are unchanged. The public derivative excludes raw scans/rasters/full OCR, signatures, identifying/contact/passport details, private-case correspondence/strategy and credentials. No outreach, mailbox access, fee, new request/filing, deletion, private push, merge or history rewrite. AveLyra commit/push verification follows the frozen public candidate separately from research completion.
